{
 "id": "2026-miskiewicz-geodiversity",
 "name": "Geodiversity and Natural Value of Stream Valleys (Photo Choice + Element Rating)",
 "description": "Faithful replication of Miśkiewicz, K., Waśkowska, A., & Stadnik, R. (2026). Perception of Geodiversity as a Factor Shaping the Value of Environmental Services and Sustainability: A Case Study of the Gościbia Forest Nature Reserve in the Carpathians (Poland). Sustainability 18:11403, doi:10.3390/su182111403. The questionnaire from Supplement S1 with its 12 photographs: four pairs of stream-valley photographs (Option 1 = lower, Option 2 = higher expert-assessed geodiversity; \"Which valley do you consider to have greater natural value?\"), four photographs of high-geodiversity sites where respondents rate how interesting 8–10 landscape elements are (valley shape, rock, rock texture, waterfall, stream, vegetation, colour, visual aesthetics, atmosphere, naturalness; 1–5), and main area of interest (natural sciences / humanities). Analysis as in the paper: share choosing each option per pair, mean and median interest per element, comparisons between interest groups (χ² for choices, rank tests for ratings). Photographs: Supplement S1 (CC BY 4.0), used with credit; the template is removed if the authors object. Differences from the original study: (1) the original was an online Microsoft Forms survey in Poland; this is an English version on SP-Survey with the English wording printed in Supplement S1; (2) a consent box was added; (3) pairs 1–4 share one page and each element-rating photograph has its own page; (4) photographs are taken from the supplement PDF at its resolution (about 350–550 px wide), and two photographs printed in two strips were joined.",
 "author": "Miśkiewicz, Waśkowska & Stadnik",
